{"code":"const containerTag = "repo_bifrost__e0ada33a9f0a14c5";
const memories = [
`Critical review finding (feature/custom-provider vs dev): GET /api/config/export serves secrets in plaintext. File transports/bifrost-http/handlers/config.go exportConfig/formatExportMCPConfig (~:859), governance (~:352-368), storage (~:385-396). Assembles raw structs: VK values bypass GetRedactedVirtualKeys, vector/logs store without .Redacted(), auth_config without FullyRedacted(), MCP client_configs verbatim incl ConnectionString/Headers/OauthClientSecret/TLS CA. Why: single authenticated read exfiltrates credential estate. Fix: redact export or gate behind stronger permission.`,
`Critical review finding: log-reveal endpoint collapses PII-reveal gating to log-read. Files transports/bifrost-http/handlers/logging.go:342-372 DefaultLogRedactionResolver ignores auth (_ *fasthttp.RequestCtx), :911-953 reveal handler; server.go:2426,2431 installs it when no enterprise resolver. RedactionMapping is json:"-" yet /reveal serves placeholder->original PII to any log reader. Why: every log viewer can de-redact every log. Fix: enforce reveal capability, not just log-read.`,
`Critical review finding (unconfirmed): guardrail logs_only mode silently redacts on wire. plugins/guardrails/config.go:116 accepts redaction_mode logs_only but redaction_tracker.go:85,115 only branches on RuntimeReversible; callers patterns.go:45/betterleaks.go:119 write result back into req/resp. Why: name promises logs-only but behavior mutates wire with no warning. Fix: implement mode or reject in validateConfig.`,
`Critical review finding (unconfirmed): restoreEgress restores full secrets into client-bound tool calls for ALL modes. plugins/guardrails/hooks.go:181,492-543,557-563 runs unconditionally in PostLLMHook replacing placeholders in tool_calls[].arguments from GetAllTokensToSecret() with no per-mode gate. Why: default runtime redaction reads as "secret gone" yet downstream logs/MCP/client history get full secret. Fix: gate on per-token mode (needs storing) or fix docs.`,
`High review finding (verified): OAuth postMessage accepted from any origin + auth code in DOM. ui/app/oauth-callback/page.tsx:19,28 postMessage(...,"*"); apiKeysFormFragment.tsx:255-263 handleMessage checks only event.data.type, never event.origin. Why: any page can post attacker code to Bifrost window for exchange; "*" leaks code to opener; DOM copy button exposes single-use codes. Fix: explicit window.location.origin + origin check, clear code after exchange.`,
`High review finding (verified): isDevelopmentMode() spoofable via query param, gates pprof/dev profiler. ui/lib/utils/port.ts:110-130 returns true for port 3000, localhost/127.0.0.1, or ?mode=dev/?dev=true. Consumers pprof/layout.tsx:10, devProfiler.tsx. Why: SSH tunnel/port-forward (normal access) passes localhost check; ?mode=dev flips gate on any host. Fix: remove query-param override, use build-time flag.`,
`High review finding (unconfirmed): OAuth exchange/poll return live tokens in-band. transports/bifrost-http/handlers/providers.go:1685-1693 antigravity exchange returns refresh+access+client_secret; :1712-1812 Cline poll returns refresh+access. No key_id binding, no one-time-use. Why: admin session can mint/read Google/WorkOS tokens as oracle. Fix: don't return access/client_secret; accept key_id and write server-side. Also clineOAuthWorkOSBase mutable package var no mutex = SSRF swap risk.`,
`High review finding (verified): provider Authorization headers persisted in log metadata with empty redact default. core/providers/utils/utils.go:546-582 SnapshotOutgoingHeaders snapshots all wire headers incl Authorization Bearer into BifrostContextKeyOutgoingHeaders; plugins/logging/main.go:1526-1557 persists, redacting only redact_sensitive_headers which defaults to [] (config.schema.json). Why: default config stores provider keys plaintext in MetadataParsed. Fix: default list to authorization/x-api-key/x-goog-api-key or route via IsSensitiveHeader.`,
`High review finding (unconfirmed): PreLLMHook mutates req in place leaking redacted text into fallbacks; MCP path skips CEL. plugins/guardrails/hooks.go:202-321 applyRulesToRequest rewrites shared *BifrostRequest; fallbacks re-execute pipeline with same object so fallback gets [SECRET-n] and its block rules never fire. mcp.go:11-56 never calls ruleMatches. Why: degraded fallback input + policy bypass. Fix: redact per-attempt from pristine copy; add missing CEL gate.`,
`High review finding (unconfirmed): GET /api/keys omits antigravity_key_config; GenerateKeyHash blind to Cline rotation. lib/config.go:7024 GetAllKeys has Cline/Databricks/GithubCopilot blocks but no Antigravity block -> credential-less render, round-trip null wipes columns in BeforeSave. clientconfig.go:884 GenerateKeyHash hashes Antigravity but not ClineKeyConfig/UseOpenAIEndpoints -> config.json rotation undetected, stale revoked token served. Fix: add missing copy + hash fields (+Antigravity in fallback structs ~1690,~1775).`,
`High review finding (unconfirmed): circuit breaker trips wrong key, never untrips, unclamped cooldown. plugins/circuitbreaker/plugin.go:93-97 keys trip off ExtraFields.Provider/ResolvedModelUsed which mixes primary-model with fallback-provider (see adaptiverouting/plugin.go:401-408) -> use GetResponseRoutingInfo. No success path so 5h DefaultCooldown sticks; resolveCooldown prefers provider-controlled "try again in X" text with no clamp -> year-long blackhole. Fix: RoutingInfo attribution + success reset + max clamp.`,
`High review finding (verified parts): openrouterfree validation + nil-deref + identity bugs. core/providers/openrouterfree/openrouterfree.go:209,217-220 validate path swallows transport errors -> outage = empty success; :160,166 provider.logger.Debug nil panic (mirror cline warn); :297 request.Unfiltered nil deref (use request!=nil check like opencodezenfree:251); :451 stream passes schemas.OpenRouter not GetProviderKey; :270-300 pipeline uses OpenRouter key stripping openrouter/ emitting wrong IDs for openrouter-free. Fix each.`,
`High review finding (unconfirmed): logging error-row backfill can persist pre-redaction payloads. plugins/logging/main.go:1917-1925,2344-2356 content_logging_on_error forces RawRequest/RawResponse from ExtraFields on guardrail 400 block. Why: provider-native bytes may predate normalized-request redaction -> blocked secret stored verbatim in most likely row. Fix: pass backfill through ApplyLiteralReplacements with redaction maps.`,
`Medium review finding (verified mechanism): updateConfig PUT full-replace wipes omitted fields incl header-redaction list. transports/bifrost-http/handlers/config.go:1228,1311 ContentLoggingOnError bool + RedactSensitiveHeaders slice decode to zero when absent -> partial update/older UI clears redaction list re-exposing finding 8. Why: plain-field assignment widens wipe surface. Fix: pointer fields nil=unchanged or field mask.`,
`Medium review finding (unconfirmed): formatExportProviderConfig drops new key types, lossy round-trip. handlers/config.go:513-575 handles Azure/Vertex/Bedrock/Ollama/VLLM/Replicate/SGL only, no Antigravity/Cline/GithubCopilot/Databricks -> export->reimport silently drops OAuth blocks. Why: hand-enumerated subset drifts. Fix: serialize already-redacted key struct directly.`,
`Medium review finding (unconfirmed): migration destroys Antigravity OAuth material without vault backup check. framework/configstore/migrations.go:13938 migrationCleanupAntigravityOAuthKeys discards vault-remove errors then NULLs value/antigravity_access_token. With vault read_only/unreachable/never-vaulted, only copy destroyed, rollback refuses. Fix: gate NULL-out on vault ref resolving or skip when !VaultStoreWriteEnabled().`,
`Medium review finding (unconfirmed): Cline BeforeSave wipes refresh token on unrelated edits. framework/configstore/tables/key.go:609-624 NULLs ClineClientID/RefreshToken when incoming config absent without ShouldPreserveStored/IsMaskedPlaceholder guard. Why: round-trip from GET /api/keys (redacted) bricks key until WorkOS device flow redone. Fix: skip nil-out on masked/empty over stored value.`,
`Medium review finding (unconfirmed): adaptive-routing updateConfig has zero validation. transports/bifrost-http/handlers/adaptiverouting.go:75-101 accepts negative ExplorationFloor, Alpha<=0|>1, negative penalties, zero TuningInterval/WindowSize, applies live via recomputeActiveWeights + persists. Why: one bad write degrades all traffic routing. Fix: mirror routing.go validation.`,
`Medium review finding (verified): -free fold suffix-strip precedes membership check; :free match unanchored. framework/modelcatalog/datasheet/types.go:410-490 normalizeProvider strips any -free before known-set check -> future custom *-free folds onto missing base; store.go:505 isFreeTierModel uses Contains(model,":free") claiming paid namespaced models. Fix: guard strip with set membership; anchor to HasSuffix(model,":free").`,
`Medium review finding (unconfirmed): routing priority schema/handler contradiction + group_adaptive dedup ignores model. config.schema.json:~4074 requires weight max1 while handlers/routing.go:761-765,895-899 rewrites missing/0 to 1.0 and ignores for priority. provKey=provider|keyID (:399) collapses multi-model cards after normalizeRoutingTargets expansion. Fix: align schema/handler; include card identity in dedup key.`,
`Medium UI finding (verified): Cline device-flow ignores server interval, polls every 1s. ui/app/workspace/providers/fragments/apiKeysFormFragment.tsx:341,347-349 hardcodes 1s, never reads ClineDeviceChallenge.interval (WorkOS minimum). Why: 5x too fast under slow_down/load for 300s risks throttling flow to failure. Fix: Math.max(1000,(interval||1)*1000) + backoff.`,
`Medium UI finding (unconfirmed): extra-detection secret inputs destroy env refs. ui/app/_fallbacks/enterprise/components/extra-detection/extraDetectionView.tsx:78-94,180-184,337-342 readSecretValue/writeSecretValue collapses {value,ref,type} to bare string -> opening with ref env.OPENAI_KEY then saving persists literal. Fix: use SecretVarInput + secretVarForm helpers.`,
`Medium UI finding (unconfirmed): new quota/reveal queries lack cache tags. ui/lib/store/apis/providersApi.ts getKeyQuota/getModelsQuota, logsApi.ts getLogRevealMapping declare no providesTags, no mutation invalidates -> stale quota after rotation. Adaptive/vault endpoints tag correctly. Fix: providesTags ProviderKeys/Quota + Logs-scoped tag.`,
`Medium review finding (verified): Groq wrong RequestType string. core/providers/groq/groq.go:106,113 passes "text completion" (space) not schemas.TextCompletionRequest/StreamRequest; branch touched lines changing "groq"->GetProviderKey() carrying typo. Why: indistinguishable methods in telemetry, misses text_completion filters. Fix: use schema constants.`,
`Medium review finding (unconfirmed): Redact mask path no bookkeeping + map aliasing. plugins/guardrails/redaction_tracker.go:101-102 mask returns Repeat("*") early with no token maps -> logging reveal + restoreEgress skip mask rules; :84-91,115-119 mutates shared redactionData maps then stores struct by value aliasing maps defeating Clone discipline in schemas/redaction.go. Fix: register token->masked; clone before SetRedactionDataOnContext.`,
`Low review note (verified by diff): ~17 template OpenAI-compatible providers clean. aisure/byteplus/dahl/gorouter/hcnsec/inferx/longcat/modal/morphllm/neuralwatt/poolside/seekai/tokenfaucet/tokenharbor/tokenrouter/vyceai/bitdeer differ only in package/ctor names, keys, base URLs; all use streamingClient for streams, delegate concurrency to openai.HandleOpenAI helpers. One live-check: modal pairs /v1-prefixed base with /v1 paths (double /v1?).`,
`Low review note (unconfirmed): reversible.go dead code blesses unsafe pattern. plugins/guardrails/reversible.go storeReversibleToken/detokenize* zero non-test callers (live path is restoreEgress); reversibleMaps comment endorses keying by *BifrostContext pointer (unsafe with pooled contexts) + raw map into ctx without mutex; hash.go [SECRET:] format wouldn't match restoreEgress. Fix: delete file + unused hashRedaction/redact*InPlace.`,
`Low review note (unsure): SecretVar.GetValue memoizes into shared struct. core/schemas/secretvar.go:527-542 writes resolved secret into e.Val on first read; Key pointers shared across requests -> concurrent first-touch race (benign value-wise) + future writer could serialize Val plaintext. Fix: go test -race on concurrent GetValue; audit no path marshals Val directly.`,
`Low review note (unconfirmed): isKeylessProvider hardcodes opencode-zen-free; GetKeyPoolFilter first-wins. server.go:1142-1150 bypasses CustomProviderConfig.IsKeyLess; lib/config.go:5919-5931 returns first LLM plugin with KeyPoolFilter (today only adaptiverouting) so future governance/circuitbreaker filter silently loses; Bootstrap captures filter once, ReloadPlugin doesn't refresh -> stale filter. Fix: drive from config, chain/document filters, refresh on reload.`,
`Low review hardening (unconfirmed): circuitbreaker per-call regex compile, TargetID re-parse, doWithContext pooled-object share, estimateFromCount NaN. parser.go:93-97 compiles 4 regexes per 429; adaptiverouting/store.go:237-268 String()/parseTargetIDString on first "/" creates phantom targets; extradetection/httpclient.go:53-78 abandoned DoTimeout writes into released fasthttp objects (buffered chan stops leak not race); counting.go:266-271 +0.999999 ceil + NaN PaddingRatio survives normalize (NaN<0 false). Fix: hoist regexes, delimiter-safe encoding, non-pooled objects for counting, IsNaN/IsInf guard + cap.`
];
let conversation_id = undefined;
const saved = [];
// First call without conversation_id to obtain it
const first = await tools.supermemory.add_memory({content: memories[0], containerTag});
conversation_id = first.conversation_id || first.conversationId || undefined;
saved.push({index: 0, id: first.id, conversation_id: conversation_id ? "got" : "missing"});
for (let i = 1; i < memories.length; i++) {
  const r = await tools.supermemory.add_memory({content: memories[i], containerTag, conversation_id});
  saved.push({index: i, id: r.id});
}
return JSON.stringify({total: memories.length, saved: saved.length, ids: saved.map(s=>s.id)});"}
